A '''tincture''' is an item that can be equipped in a [[flask]] slot and activated to enhance the user's melee [[weapon]]s with special bonuses. While active, they inflict Mana Burn on the user, causing [[mana]] [[loss]] over time at an accelerating rate, and will automatically deactivate when you reach 0 mana. By default, you can only have one tincture active at a time.

==Mechanics==
Upon using a tincture, it activates the tincture, granting its effects. While a tincture is active, you gain stacks of Mana Burn over time. {{c|help|Mana Burn causes you to lose 1% of your maximum Mana per stack per second.}} A stack of Mana Burn will always drain a minimum of 1 mana. Tinctures deactivate when manually deactivated or when you reach 0 mana. Once a tincture is deactivated, it procs a cooldown on all tinctures, preventing you from activating any tincture for the duration. The rate at which you gain Mana Burn and the duration of the cooldown depends on the tincture base type and associated stats and modifiers.

:[[Bloodsoaked Blade]] will cause Mana Burn and all associated effects to instead apply Weeping Wounds, which is identical to Mana Burn except that it drains 1% of maximum life per stack per second instead.

Due to the server tick rate of 33 milliseconds, it is impossible to indefinitely sustain Tinctures even if you have infinite mana recovery (or life recovery with [[Bloodsoaked Blade]]) once the resource degeneration crosses a certain threshold. The exact degeneration needed to deplete your whole resource pool in one tick is given by the formula {{math|formula=
Degen(U) = {1000 * U \over 33 }
}}, where Degen is the total degeneration (inclusive of other sources not limited to Mana Burn or Weeping Wounds) and U is your unreserved resource pool. For example, with 100 unreserved maximum mana, you would need to degenerate 3030.30 mana per second to deplete your unreserved mana pool in one tick.

The resource drain per stack of Mana Drain or Weeping Wounds is given by the formula {{math|formula=
Drain(R) = {max(0.01 * R, 1)}
}}, where R is your maximum resource pool. For the purposes of minimizing the drain from either Mana Drain or Weeping Wounds, there is no benefit to decreasing the maximum resource pool below 100. 

With S stacks of either Mana Drain or Weeping Wounds, the total resource drain per second is {{math|formula=
S * {max(0.01 * R, 1)}
}}, and thus to instantly empty the pool in one tick, the maximum stacks you can have given infinite resource recovery is {{math|formula=
S(U, R) = {1000 * U \over 33 * max(0.01 * R, 1)}
}}.

Tincture effects only apply to [[attack]]s with your [[weapon]]s, including from [[proxies]] like {{il|Blade Trap}} or [[ballista]]s. The stats from Tinctures are not [[local]] to weapons, but are specifically restricted to only apply to weapon attacks. Tinctures apply to both weapons while [[dual-wielding]]. [[Minion]]s which use your weapon, such as with {{il|The Dancing Dervish}} or {{il|The Iron Mass}}, do not benefit from tinctures.

Tinctures only affect melee weapon attacks by default, though this includes projectile skills that use melee weapons, such as {{il|Spectral Throw}} and {{il|Splitting Steel}}. Tinctures do not apply to [[wand]]s or [[bow]]s unless [[Warden]]'s [[Seasoned Hunter]] passive skill has been allocated. Tinctures can never affect non-weapon hits, including [[spell]]s, [[Unarmed]] attacks, and [[shield]] skills.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3452002#4|title=Path of Exile 2 and Path of Exile: Affliction Recently Asked Questions|date=December 3, 2023|accessdate=December 3, 2023}}</ref>

By default, only a single tincture effect can be active at a time, though multiple tinctures can be equipped. The number of active tinctures you can have at a time can be increased with the following:
* {{psl|Experienced Herbalist}} ([[Warden]]) (+1)
* {{psl|id=AscendancyAscendant34}} ([[Ascendant]]) (+1)
* {{il|The Living Blade}} (+2)
* [[Martial Weapon Display]] in [[version 3.30.0]] ([[Reliquarian]]) (+2)

Tinctures can only be {{c|normal|normal}}, {{c|magic|magic}}, or {{c|unique|unique}}. There are no {{c|rare|rare}} tinctures. Tinctures can be given [[quality]] with a {{il|Glassblower's Bauble}}, granting 1% more Tincture Effect per quality.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3532389#40</ref>

All modifiers from tinctures that have effects when killing an enemy only apply to [[killing blow]]s (hits) from weapons while a tincture is active. It does not apply to kills from [[damage over time]].

Tinctures are not considered [[flask]]s and can be used in the fifth flask slot while having a {{il|Micro-Distillery Belt}} equipped without any downsides.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3452002#10</ref> Tinctures are considered as occupying a flask slot for the purposes of [[The Traitor (keystone passive)|The Traitor]] or [[Intensifying Suffusion]].

